1
00:00:01,502 --> 00:00:02,970
♪♪

2
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:43,161
Oh, look, antelope.

3
00:01:43,303 --> 00:01:44,703
They're cows.

4
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:48,036
Ben, we're in the middle of
Nevada. They're antelope.

5
00:01:48,175 --> 00:01:49,175
Cows.

6
00:01:49,242 --> 00:01:51,177
Oh, stop being a
stick in the mud.

7
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:53,473
Well, it's just I don't get it.

8
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:55,344
You go to this charity auction,

9
00:01:55,482 --> 00:01:57,542
and of all the trips
you could have bid on,

10
00:01:57,684 --> 00:01:59,812
you had to wind
up with this one.

11
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,616
Because I thought that
spending the weekend

12
00:02:02,756 --> 00:02:06,386
with a bunch of friends at a
dude ranch sounded like fun,

13
00:02:06,526 --> 00:02:08,995
and I haven't thrown
a party in a long time,

14
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:11,064
and the money went
for a good cause.

15
00:02:11,198 --> 00:02:14,396
And as luck would have
it, nobody else bid on it.

16
00:02:14,534 --> 00:02:17,163
There's going to be horses.

17
00:02:18,438 --> 00:02:22,307
Of course there's going to
be horses. It's a dude ranch.

18
00:02:22,442 --> 00:02:25,571
I don't know how
to ride one of them.

19
00:02:25,712 --> 00:02:27,738
Well, you'll learn.

20
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:31,211
I'm not going to
get on one of them.

21
00:02:31,351 --> 00:02:32,546
Oh, Ben.

22
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:37,450
I'm afraid of horses.

23
00:03:18,732 --> 00:03:21,702
May as well get out and
stretch your legs, folks.

24
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,728
Oh, wow.

25
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:26,271
This is great.

26
00:03:30,844 --> 00:03:35,282
Reminds me of a mini-mall my
ex-brother-in-law talked me into buying.

27
00:03:47,194 --> 00:03:50,687
Well, this isn't the
dude ranch, is it, Julie?

28
00:03:50,831 --> 00:03:54,768
No. I'm sure the driver's just
taking a break or something.

29
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:59,100
Either that, or he's looking
for a fire extinguisher.

30
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:00,605
Oh, Ben.

31
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:02,869
Let me go see what's going on.

32
00:04:04,945 --> 00:04:06,345
What's the trouble?

33
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,971
Engine's overheating.

34
00:04:08,115 --> 00:04:09,947
Any reason why?

35
00:04:13,854 --> 00:04:15,083
We're out of oil.

36
00:04:15,222 --> 00:04:16,781
Out of oil?

37
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:17,923
Yep.

38
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:23,859
The crank case is
leaking like a sieve.

39
00:04:23,997 --> 00:04:26,592
How long is it going
to take you to fix it?

40
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:31,661
My job is to drive
this bus, not to fix it.

41
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:34,138
Well, what are you
going to do about it?

42
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:37,267
Get on the radio, tell the boss
to send a mechanic out here.

43
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:39,777
May as well make
yourselves comfortable, folks.

44
00:04:39,913 --> 00:04:41,779
Looks like we're going
to be here a while.

45
00:04:41,915 --> 00:04:43,884
It's okay. He's got a radio.

46
00:04:44,017 --> 00:04:47,078
It's not like we're going to be
stranded here for days or anything.

47
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,054
Come on, you
guys. It will be fun.

48
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:53,183
Now, who wants to go exploring?

49
00:04:53,326 --> 00:04:54,385
Oh, hey, hey.

50
00:04:54,528 --> 00:04:59,159
I vote we find a nice shady tree
and play a little game of chance.

51
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:00,790
Have a few cold ones.

52
00:05:00,934 --> 00:05:02,732
Now you're talking.

53
00:05:02,869 --> 00:05:04,531
Come on, let's look around.

54
00:05:04,671 --> 00:05:06,765
- Want to go with us?
- No, thanks.

55
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:12,804
Hey, Ben, Julie... come
here. You've got to see this.

56
00:06:07,334 --> 00:06:09,496
You're blocking the door.

57
00:06:29,789 --> 00:06:32,020
♪♪

58
00:06:51,177 --> 00:06:52,736
What will it be?

59
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,189
Who is the sheriff talking to?

60
00:07:03,223 --> 00:07:04,987
That's Ned Salem.

61
00:07:05,125 --> 00:07:09,563
The cardshark's Gil
Brisco. Must be new in town.

62
00:07:12,999 --> 00:07:14,490
That's old Bob...

63
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:16,960
Yep.

64
00:07:20,006 --> 00:07:23,170
Dead drunk, the same as always.

65
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:26,212
Well, well, I don't believe
I've had the pleasure.

66
00:07:26,346 --> 00:07:28,781
Welcome to Golden
Springs, stranger.

67
00:07:28,915 --> 00:07:30,781
My name's Michelle.

68
00:07:30,917 --> 00:07:32,545
What's yours?

69
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,020
I need to talk to you.

70
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:38,284
It will have to wait. I'm busy.

71
00:07:38,425 --> 00:07:39,620
Miss Thomas!

72
00:07:52,172 --> 00:07:54,198
I just heard about Willis.

73
00:07:54,341 --> 00:07:56,970
He drew on me, Conrad.

74
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:59,102
Drew on me and lost.

75
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:04,041
Here's what I'm
going to do, Sheriff.

76
00:08:04,184 --> 00:08:07,086
First I'm going to step over
to that bar and get me a drink.

77
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:11,852
Then I'm going to go get my gun,
and I'm going to come looking for you.

78
00:08:13,259 --> 00:08:14,386
You do...

79
00:08:15,795 --> 00:08:18,162
you're going to wind
up just like your uncle...

80
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:21,999
Dead.

81
00:08:31,678 --> 00:08:33,169
Whiskey.

82
00:08:35,715 --> 00:08:39,311
Not that stuff, the
good stuff under here.

83
00:08:39,452 --> 00:08:43,116
Don't never let him pour from them
bottles up there... he waters them down.

84
00:08:43,256 --> 00:08:45,851
Thanks for the tip.

85
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:48,018
I'm Ben Matlock.

86
00:08:52,665 --> 00:08:55,066
Conrad McMasters.

87
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,601
New in these parts?

88
00:08:56,736 --> 00:08:58,637
Real new.

89
00:08:58,772 --> 00:09:00,240
Where are you staying?

90
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,773
I don't know yet.

91
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:04,173
Any suggestions?

92
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:07,144
Julie's Boarding House,
right down the street.

93
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:09,272
She's about to have a vacancy.

94
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:11,282
She is?

95
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:13,080
Her brother's room.

96
00:09:14,487 --> 00:09:16,046
He's the sheriff.

97
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:40,979
Morning.

98
00:09:41,114 --> 00:09:42,548
Hi.

99
00:09:42,682 --> 00:09:44,310
Are you Julie?

100
00:09:44,451 --> 00:09:47,512
You must be the stranger
my brother told me about.

101
00:09:47,654 --> 00:09:49,054
Need a room, do you?

102
00:09:49,189 --> 00:09:51,158
As a matter of fact, I do.

103
00:09:51,291 --> 00:09:53,692
Going to be in town long?

104
00:09:53,827 --> 00:09:56,092
I'm not really sure.

105
00:09:59,232 --> 00:10:00,598
This here's your room.

106
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:03,601
It will cost you a
dollar a day in advance.

107
00:10:03,736 --> 00:10:05,329
A dollar?

108
00:10:05,472 --> 00:10:07,839
That includes meals, of course.

109
00:10:07,974 --> 00:10:08,974
Oh.

110
00:10:09,042 --> 00:10:11,671
Oh, I'll take it.

111
00:10:11,811 --> 00:10:13,939
Uh, will some of these do?

112
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,742
My Lord!

113
00:10:15,882 --> 00:10:19,046
I'm renting you a room,
not selling you the place.

114
00:10:19,185 --> 00:10:21,916
This is just fine.

115
00:10:22,055 --> 00:10:26,151
Well, you've got yourself room
and board now for five days.

116
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,292
Oh.

117
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:31,092
You, uh, with
the railroad, Mr...?

118
00:10:31,231 --> 00:10:33,427
Matlock. No, I'm not.

119
00:10:33,566 --> 00:10:38,470
Men who carry all that cash
usually work for the railroad...

120
00:10:38,605 --> 00:10:41,074
Or just got done robbing it.

121
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:45,339
You're no outlaw,
are you, Mr. Matlock?

122
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:48,073
No, no. I'm a lawyer.

123
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:53,753
I'll just get you some
water so you can wash up.

124
00:10:53,887 --> 00:11:00,316
Uh, actually right now, I'm more
interested in using the facilities.

125
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:04,858
You know, the restroom.

126
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:08,196
The men's...

127
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:13,272
Oh, of course.
It's right out back.

128
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:15,298
Out back?

129
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:31,287
I ain't going to tell you
but one time, Sheriff.

130
00:11:31,424 --> 00:11:34,258
If you don't stop messing
in my affairs, tin badge or no,

131
00:11:34,394 --> 00:11:36,454
you're going to be real
sorry. Do you hear me?

132
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:58,616
Where's the sheriff?

133
00:12:00,353 --> 00:12:01,787
At the jail.

134
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:06,954
Hey, Willis is a no-good
troublemaker, Conrad.

135
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:09,494
He ain't worth dying
for, and you know it.

136
00:12:11,731 --> 00:12:14,326
A man's got to do
what a man's got to do.

137
00:12:21,841 --> 00:12:23,810
Get your gun on.

138
00:12:23,943 --> 00:12:26,538
You don't want
to do this, Conrad.

139
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:28,341
You killed my uncle.

140
00:12:28,481 --> 00:12:30,279
You didn't even like your uncle.

141
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,351
He raised me.

142
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:34,317
I owe him.

143
00:12:34,454 --> 00:12:36,821
He raised you because he
liked having somebody around

144
00:12:36,956 --> 00:12:38,116
he could kick the tar out of.

145
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:40,216
Get your gun on.

146
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:44,821
In my desk, bottom drawer.

147
00:12:57,710 --> 00:13:00,976
Some folks is just too nice
for their own damn good.

148
00:13:04,717 --> 00:13:06,310
Ohh!

149
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:21,665
Jailhouse?

150
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:22,996
Let's get down there!

151
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,814
Excuse me, please.

152
00:13:35,948 --> 00:13:38,782
Excuse me. Excuse me.
Excuse me. Excuse me.

153
00:13:41,921 --> 00:13:43,389
Excuse me. Excuse me.

154
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:47,290
Uh, excuse me. Could I
just slip through this, in here?

155
00:13:54,734 --> 00:13:55,861
Come on. Let's go.

156
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,369
- But I didn't kill him.
- Come on.

157
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,699
I didn't do it.

158
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:02,399
Somebody's got to
believe me. I didn't kill him.

159
00:14:07,113 --> 00:14:08,513
I'm innocent.

160
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:22,188
I guess he clobbered me,

161
00:14:22,328 --> 00:14:25,696
because the next thing I
know, I'm lying on the floor

162
00:14:25,832 --> 00:14:29,462
and he's lying across from
me with a big hole in his chest.

163
00:14:29,602 --> 00:14:31,002
Where was your gun?

164
00:14:31,137 --> 00:14:32,628
In my hand.

165
00:14:32,772 --> 00:14:35,742
And I don't know how
it got there, I swear.

166
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,969
Then what happened?

167
00:14:38,111 --> 00:14:40,842
I got up to take a
look at the sheriff,

168
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:43,313
and then the deputy
comes in and starts hollering.

169
00:14:43,449 --> 00:14:45,179
You mean the deputy came in

170
00:14:45,318 --> 00:14:48,254
and saw you standing over the
sheriff with the gun in your hand?

171
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,720
Yes.

172
00:14:49,856 --> 00:14:53,315
Oh.

173
00:14:53,459 --> 00:14:55,860
Are there any
lawyers in this town?

174
00:14:55,995 --> 00:14:58,521
There used to, but it seems like
people always get mad at them

175
00:14:58,664 --> 00:14:59,791
and wind up shooting them.

176
00:15:02,101 --> 00:15:03,729
Damn it, Willis!

177
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:05,498
If I'd have just shot him myself

178
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,249
instead of waiting around
for the sheriff to do it,

179
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:08,639
none of this would
have happened.

180
00:15:08,775 --> 00:15:09,970
I thought he was your uncle.

181
00:15:10,109 --> 00:15:11,787
He was the meanest man
that ever walked this earth.

182
00:15:11,811 --> 00:15:14,747
Well, why did you go
after the sheriff like that?

183
00:15:17,049 --> 00:15:18,677
Willis was family.

184
00:15:18,818 --> 00:15:21,049
A man's got to do
what a man's got to do.

185
00:15:24,557 --> 00:15:26,219
Why is that?

186
00:15:26,359 --> 00:15:27,622
Why is what?

187
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:32,130
Why does a man got to
do what a man's got to do?

188
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:36,794
Do you realize how many people
have been killed in John Wayne movies

189
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:38,962
all because of that one line?

190
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:44,169
Men, women, children,
towns, villages, forts...

191
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:47,838
All wiped out because
somebody strapped on a gun

192
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:51,576
and said a man's got to
do what a man's got to do.

193
00:15:51,717 --> 00:15:55,051
Somebody should have
jerked that jackass around

194
00:15:55,188 --> 00:15:57,657
and knocked the
living hell out of him.

195
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:01,283
A man's got to do
what a man's got to do.

196
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:09,268
Well, if you want me
to take your case, I will.

197
00:16:09,402 --> 00:16:11,837
As it happens, I'm a lawyer.

198
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:14,667
How come?

199
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,673
I like being a lawyer.

200
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:20,541
No, how come you'll take my
case? You don't hardly even know me.

201
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,706
I don't know.

202
00:16:22,849 --> 00:16:26,877
Somewhere in my
mind I feel like I do.

203
00:16:27,019 --> 00:16:29,887
Well, I can't pay you much.

204
00:16:30,022 --> 00:16:32,617
The fact is I can't
pay you nothing.

205
00:16:32,758 --> 00:16:35,660
You don't have to pay me.

206
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:39,228
Just don't shoot me.

207
00:16:43,269 --> 00:16:47,673
Any idea what time it was
when you heard the shot?

208
00:16:47,807 --> 00:16:49,503
I didn't hear no shot.

209
00:16:49,642 --> 00:16:51,907
You didn't?

210
00:16:52,044 --> 00:16:56,948
A gun this big, I'd think you could
hear the shot all the way to California.

211
00:16:57,083 --> 00:16:58,608
There's five bullets.

212
00:16:58,751 --> 00:17:01,482
The sixth one went through the
sheriff and stuck in the wall there.

213
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:04,231
You are going to run
ballistics to make sure

214
00:17:04,255 --> 00:17:06,889
the bullet came out
of this gun, aren't you?

215
00:17:08,261 --> 00:17:09,456
I'm going to do what?

216
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:14,766
Uh, you're going to, uh...

217
00:17:14,901 --> 00:17:17,871
run a full investigation?

218
00:17:18,004 --> 00:17:20,132
Well, Conrad said he
was going to get the sheriff.

219
00:17:20,273 --> 00:17:21,502
That's what he done.

220
00:17:21,641 --> 00:17:23,769
Of course, if the sheriff
had been wearing his gun,

221
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,187
that would have
been self-defense.

222
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:29,478
But since he weren't, that just
makes it cold-blooded murder.

223
00:17:29,615 --> 00:17:32,847
Cut and dried, just the way
the circuit court judge likes it.

224
00:17:32,985 --> 00:17:36,513
Uh, Ned Salem...

225
00:17:36,656 --> 00:17:43,495
I saw him out behind the boarding
house today giving the sheriff what for.

226
00:17:43,629 --> 00:17:46,269
The sheriff was probably talking
to him about that cattle rustling.

227
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:48,867
What cattle rustling?

228
00:17:49,001 --> 00:17:50,993
The rustling he
thought Ned was doing.

229
00:17:52,271 --> 00:17:54,740
Where can I find Ned Salem?

230
00:17:54,874 --> 00:17:56,399
At his ranch, I expect.

231
00:17:56,542 --> 00:17:59,637
It's the Lazy B. It's about
an hour's ride north of town.

232
00:17:59,779 --> 00:18:02,078
Hour's ride.

233
00:18:07,286 --> 00:18:08,720
Let's be friends.

234
00:18:08,854 --> 00:18:09,878
Come on.

235
00:18:10,022 --> 00:18:15,552
Now, I'm kind of
new at this, so I'll...

236
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:20,063
So I'll take all
the help I can get.

237
00:18:20,199 --> 00:18:23,328
Now, you... There
you go, that's a boy.

238
00:18:23,469 --> 00:18:25,904
Yeah. Now you stay right here.

239
00:18:26,038 --> 00:18:29,099
Stand still, and
I'm gonna... get on.

240
00:18:40,753 --> 00:18:43,086
I nearly got it. There.

241
00:18:43,222 --> 00:18:44,417
No.

242
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,829
Would you stand
real still, and I'll...

243
00:18:58,404 --> 00:19:01,272
Could you... Could you just...

244
00:19:03,175 --> 00:19:06,145
Wait. Wait. Wait. Wait.

245
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:14,185
Hold still. Hold still. Hold
still. Hold still. Hold still.

246
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,583
Wait.

247
00:19:29,368 --> 00:19:30,768
Giddyup.

248
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:33,165
Come on.

249
00:19:33,305 --> 00:19:36,070
Come on, come on. Giddyup.

250
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:37,540
Come on.

251
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:46,884
No. No. No. No.

252
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:50,421
Oh, no. No. No. Whoa.

253
00:19:54,493 --> 00:19:57,019
Let Captain Stewart take
his pick from this bunch,

254
00:19:57,163 --> 00:20:00,759
but make sure the ones we take him
come from that herd down by the river.

255
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,028
Man thinks he knows
his cattle, but he don't.

256
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:04,169
Come on, run.

257
00:20:04,236 --> 00:20:06,728
Oh, this saddle is getting...

258
00:20:06,872 --> 00:20:09,808
Is getting a little
hard, Brownie.

259
00:20:11,644 --> 00:20:14,239
We're getting close, Brownie.

260
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,372
We're going to
get them. Come on.

261
00:20:16,515 --> 00:20:18,313
Mr. Salem?

262
00:20:19,919 --> 00:20:21,751
I'm Ben Matlock.

263
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:24,413
Oh, I've seen you
earlier, in the saloon.

264
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:28,153
You know, if you come to town to buy
some beef, you've come to the right place.

265
00:20:28,294 --> 00:20:31,128
Oh, no, no. I'm not buying.

266
00:20:31,263 --> 00:20:32,959
I'm... I'm a lawyer.

267
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,130
Too bad.

268
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:40,330
Lawyers don't seem to
fare too well around here.

269
00:20:40,473 --> 00:20:42,169
That's what I heard.

270
00:20:42,308 --> 00:20:46,973
Anyway, I'm representing the
man accused of killing the sheriff.

271
00:20:47,113 --> 00:20:50,550
Oh, that's a terrible thing.
The sheriff was a good man.

272
00:20:50,683 --> 00:20:56,782
Yeah. I understand that he suspects you of
coming by some of these cattle illegally.

273
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:59,482
I ain't no cattle rustler,
and the sheriff knew it.

274
00:20:59,625 --> 00:21:03,357
Why, him and me was friends.

275
00:21:04,663 --> 00:21:08,930
It didn't sound like it from what I
heard behind the boarding house today.

276
00:21:09,068 --> 00:21:10,366
Now you look here.

277
00:21:10,503 --> 00:21:13,166
I run a big outfit
here, and I run it right.

278
00:21:13,305 --> 00:21:16,605
The army over at Fort Rye
wants beef, they buy it from me.

279
00:21:16,742 --> 00:21:18,142
I got me a contract.

280
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:19,973
I got lots of contracts.

281
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:22,274
Now, some of the
ranchers don't like that,

282
00:21:22,414 --> 00:21:25,782
so they try to make me look bad
by accusing me of things I didn't do.

283
00:21:25,918 --> 00:21:27,614
Oh, yeah.

284
00:21:27,753 --> 00:21:31,554
It's just that you were so mad,

285
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:36,287
and then, an hour
later, he was so dead.

286
00:21:37,429 --> 00:21:41,025
Well, I wasn't mad enough to kill
him, if that's what you're getting at.

287
00:21:42,434 --> 00:21:46,064
McMasters, now
he was mad enough.

288
00:21:46,205 --> 00:21:47,537
Brisco, too.

289
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:49,642
- Gil Brisco?
- Yeah.

290
00:21:49,775 --> 00:21:53,109
Sheriff threw him in the
hoosgow for cheating last week

291
00:21:53,245 --> 00:21:57,979
just when a bunch of miners he was looking
forward to gamble with come to town.

292
00:21:58,117 --> 00:22:00,882
Well, Gil Brisco
was fit to be tied.

293
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:02,955
- Swore he'd get even.
- Oh?

294
00:22:03,088 --> 00:22:05,421
Well, I appreciate the tip.

295
00:22:05,558 --> 00:22:07,151
Glad to help.

296
00:22:07,293 --> 00:22:08,784
Come on, Brownie.

297
00:22:08,928 --> 00:22:10,191
Come on.

298
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,729
Come on, Brownie.

299
00:22:11,864 --> 00:22:13,594
Come on, come on, come on.

300
00:22:13,732 --> 00:22:15,530
Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh!

301
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:21,107
You ain't going to do this for a whole
hour, are you... are you, Brownie?

302
00:22:25,711 --> 00:22:27,703
Hey, Mr. Brisco.

303
00:22:27,847 --> 00:22:30,874
Hey. Ben Matlock.

304
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:33,008
Oh, yes, of course.

305
00:22:33,152 --> 00:22:36,088
Word gets around fast in
Golden Springs, Mr. Matlock.

306
00:22:36,222 --> 00:22:37,690
- Pleased to meet you.
- Yes.

307
00:22:37,823 --> 00:22:41,851
You know, I don't think I've ever
seen a lawyer up close before...

308
00:22:41,994 --> 00:22:43,826
Not a live one, at least.

309
00:22:44,830 --> 00:22:46,093
Oh.

310
00:22:49,134 --> 00:22:51,660
I'd like to ask you
some questions.

311
00:22:51,804 --> 00:22:53,966
- Where are you from?
- Atlanta.

312
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:56,598
Do they play five card
draw down in Atlanta?

313
00:22:56,742 --> 00:22:59,541
What's that got to do with my
asking you some questions?

314
00:22:59,678 --> 00:23:04,844
Well, nothing loosens my tongue
quite like a game of cards, that's all.

315
00:23:04,984 --> 00:23:07,446
Oh. Well... Two dollar ante.

316
00:23:10,089 --> 00:23:12,581
Well, you aren't going
to cheat, are you?

317
00:23:12,725 --> 00:23:16,423
I have never cheated at
cards in my life, and I never will.

318
00:23:16,562 --> 00:23:18,463
That's the God's
honest truth, Mr. Matlock.

319
00:23:18,597 --> 00:23:21,624
Is that why the sheriff
threw you in jail last week?

320
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:25,397
He threw me in jail
because I was showing

321
00:23:25,537 --> 00:23:28,974
what he considered to be an
unhealthy interest in his sister.

322
00:23:29,108 --> 00:23:30,108
Cards.

323
00:23:30,175 --> 00:23:32,235
Accusing me of
something I never did

324
00:23:32,378 --> 00:23:34,574
and temporarily depriving
me of my livelihood

325
00:23:34,713 --> 00:23:39,674
was his clever way of telling
me to stay away from her.

326
00:23:39,818 --> 00:23:43,016
Oh. I bet that made you mad.

327
00:23:43,155 --> 00:23:45,624
Yes, it did.

328
00:23:45,758 --> 00:23:48,125
But you didn't stay
away from her?

329
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,626
Raise.

330
00:23:49,762 --> 00:23:52,027
No, I didn't.

331
00:23:52,164 --> 00:23:55,828
Is that why he wound
up dead an hour later?

332
00:24:00,406 --> 00:24:03,308
Looks like everybody
but you and me has folded.

333
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:04,933
What you got?

334
00:24:07,413 --> 00:24:08,847
Three 5s.

335
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:12,849
Three ladies.

336
00:24:16,388 --> 00:24:19,256
Where were you around
1:30 this afternoon?

337
00:24:19,391 --> 00:24:22,156
I'm afraid you're going to have
to ante up before I answer that.

338
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:25,696
You've taken
everything I've got.

339
00:24:25,831 --> 00:24:32,601
Then our conversation, though
it has been my pleasure, is over.

340
00:24:51,991 --> 00:24:54,517
Well, hello, Ben.

341
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,755
I've been expecting you.

342
00:24:57,896 --> 00:24:59,626
You have?

343
00:24:59,765 --> 00:25:01,734
I have.

344
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:05,702
I've heard all about you.

345
00:25:06,872 --> 00:25:10,832
And I just assumed in
time you'd hear all about me.

346
00:25:10,976 --> 00:25:13,207
Here, let me help you
get more comfortable.

347
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:15,007
Uh...

348
00:25:16,715 --> 00:25:19,913
Uh, uh, uh,

349
00:25:20,052 --> 00:25:22,954
I... I just came
up here to talk.

350
00:25:23,088 --> 00:25:26,786
I gambled all my money
away. I mean, every penny.

351
00:25:26,925 --> 00:25:29,656
Oh, you poor thing.

352
00:25:29,795 --> 00:25:34,563
What I mean is I can't pay you.

353
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:36,999
Oh, sure you can.

354
00:25:37,136 --> 00:25:40,913
Look, you've got these
nice silver cufflinks

355
00:25:40,937 --> 00:25:44,566
and, oh, this beautiful
gold pocket watch.

356
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:46,121
Why, if all I took around
these parts was cash,

357
00:25:46,145 --> 00:25:48,341
I'd have gone out of
business years ago.

358
00:25:50,482 --> 00:25:52,610
Um, uh...

359
00:25:52,751 --> 00:25:56,347
I... I wanted to ask
you about the sheriff.

360
00:25:57,423 --> 00:25:58,914
What about him?

361
00:25:59,058 --> 00:26:01,926
What did he want
to talk to you about?

362
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:05,589
Same thing he always wanted
to talk about... my leaving.

363
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:09,532
He was the only man in town who
wasn't pleased as pie I'd settled here.

364
00:26:09,668 --> 00:26:11,899
Of course, that's because
he was the only man in town

365
00:26:12,037 --> 00:26:14,836
who hadn't availed
himself of my services.

366
00:26:14,973 --> 00:26:19,240
He would have eventually if he
hadn't had such a prude for a sister.

367
00:26:19,378 --> 00:26:22,041
Let me just slip this right off.

368
00:26:22,181 --> 00:26:25,913
I just came up here to talk.

369
00:26:26,051 --> 00:26:31,456
And now that we've
talked, I'd just as soon leave.

370
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:35,459
See, I'm kind of a prude myself.

371
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:36,687
Wait a minute.

372
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:47,372
I'll walk you out.

373
00:26:49,241 --> 00:26:52,871
It's not often I get to
be seen with a lawyer.

374
00:26:58,117 --> 00:27:00,109
I just hope nobody shoots you.

375
00:27:03,856 --> 00:27:05,290
Hey, are you Michelle?

376
00:27:05,424 --> 00:27:08,019
I am. What's your name?

377
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:10,527
Blue. I just came
down from Hollister.

378
00:27:10,662 --> 00:27:11,662
Buy you a drink?

379
00:27:11,763 --> 00:27:13,603
Now, you didn't come
all the way from Hollister

380
00:27:13,699 --> 00:27:15,668
just to buy me a drink,
now did you, Blue?

381
00:27:15,801 --> 00:27:17,827
Hold it, Michelle. I want
to see you right now.

382
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:20,769
- Hey, wait your turn.
- Stay out of this.

383
00:28:09,454 --> 00:28:10,581
Bob?

384
00:28:11,657 --> 00:28:13,216
Bob.

385
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:14,917
Are you all right?

386
00:28:35,180 --> 00:28:38,344
You knew my brother,
and he was a good sheriff.

387
00:28:38,483 --> 00:28:43,854
There weren't no call for him to be cut
down in the prime of life by some coward.

388
00:28:43,989 --> 00:28:46,823
You... I ask you, is that fair?

389
00:28:46,959 --> 00:28:53,058
I say we do something about
it, and I say we do it now.

390
00:29:04,977 --> 00:29:06,502
Unlock it, Tom.

391
00:29:06,645 --> 00:29:08,705
Now, Miss Julie, you
know I can't do that.

392
00:29:08,847 --> 00:29:10,748
You owe my brother, Tom.

393
00:29:10,882 --> 00:29:14,978
Or did you forget how
he saved your hide

394
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:19,490
that time Lennie Canfield come out after
you for accidentally shooting his horse.

395
00:29:19,625 --> 00:29:21,753
Judge Hogelby has
already been sent for.

396
00:29:21,893 --> 00:29:24,556
If he gets here and he finds
Conrad has already been hung,

397
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:27,598
there's going to be hell to pay,
and I'm going to be the one paying it.

398
00:29:27,733 --> 00:29:29,544
Excuse me. Excuse me. Let
me through. Let me through.

399
00:29:29,568 --> 00:29:31,594
Excuse me. Let me get through.

400
00:29:31,737 --> 00:29:33,569
Watch your feet. Let me through.

401
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:35,665
You can't do this.

402
00:29:35,807 --> 00:29:37,571
Of course I can.

403
00:29:37,709 --> 00:29:38,972
He killed my brother.

404
00:29:39,111 --> 00:29:41,910
It just looks like he
killed your brother.

405
00:29:42,047 --> 00:29:44,812
Well, that's good
enough for us, isn't it?

406
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:46,111
Yeah!

407
00:29:46,251 --> 00:29:48,811
All right. All right.
All right. All right.

408
00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:54,655
You want to string him
up, okay, but two points:

409
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:59,288
1, I'm his lawyer, and
he deserves a fair trial;

410
00:29:59,431 --> 00:30:05,735
and 2, I'm a customer at your place
of business... your boarding house...

411
00:30:05,871 --> 00:30:13,108
And that's a conflict of interest and
might be viewed as against the law.

412
00:30:18,517 --> 00:30:19,985
All right, everybody out.

413
00:30:20,118 --> 00:30:22,053
Out. Out.

414
00:30:23,889 --> 00:30:27,223
Hope you like
beans, Mr. Matlock,

415
00:30:27,359 --> 00:30:30,989
because that's what you're
going to be getting for lunch.

416
00:30:32,230 --> 00:30:34,756
And dinner, more than likely.

417
00:30:36,168 --> 00:30:39,104
Breakfast, too.

418
00:30:44,810 --> 00:30:48,474
Thanks. I thought I was a
goner there for a second.

419
00:30:48,613 --> 00:30:50,081
I thought you was, too.

420
00:30:50,215 --> 00:30:53,242
I rode out to Ned Salem's place,

421
00:30:53,385 --> 00:30:58,187
and he said all this cattle
rustling stuff was just a rumor.

422
00:30:58,323 --> 00:31:01,885
Well, all I know is some cowboy
swore he saw a bunch of steers

423
00:31:02,027 --> 00:31:04,587
with a Broken Rock brand
in with Ned Salem's herd.

424
00:31:04,730 --> 00:31:07,393
Why didn't the sheriff
take a look himself?

425
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:09,558
Well, he did. He rode
there the same day.

426
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:12,068
The only brands he saw in
Salem's herd was Salem's.

427
00:31:12,204 --> 00:31:14,105
This cowboy, what's his name?

428
00:31:14,239 --> 00:31:15,832
Rudy Simms.

429
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:18,842
Do you know
where I can find him?

430
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:23,981
Whoa. Whoa. We don't
have to be in such a hurry.

431
00:31:24,116 --> 00:31:25,414
There you go.

432
00:31:28,053 --> 00:31:29,817
- Rudy Simms?
- Yeah.

433
00:31:29,955 --> 00:31:32,117
I'm Ben Matlock.

434
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:34,692
Boy, that was some
brawl, wasn't it?

435
00:31:34,826 --> 00:31:36,294
I don't remember
seeing you there.

436
00:31:36,428 --> 00:31:39,159
Well, I spent most of
my time under a table.

437
00:31:39,297 --> 00:31:42,961
I have this strong sense
of self-preservation.

438
00:31:43,101 --> 00:31:46,868
I'm trying to help
Conrad McMasters prove

439
00:31:47,005 --> 00:31:49,531
that he was not the
one who shot the sheriff.

440
00:31:49,674 --> 00:31:51,165
I'm his lawyer.

441
00:31:51,309 --> 00:31:52,436
Yeah?

442
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:54,773
Well, I hear that
you told the sheriff

443
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:58,213
that you thought Ned
Salem had stolen some cattle.

444
00:31:58,350 --> 00:32:00,285
Yep, that's right.

445
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:02,888
Do you want to tell
me how that happened?

446
00:32:04,055 --> 00:32:06,923
Well, you know last time it
rained about a week ago?

447
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:12,190
Actually, I'm kind of new
in town, so no, I don't.

448
00:32:12,330 --> 00:32:13,559
But go on.

449
00:32:13,698 --> 00:32:15,860
Well, I was riding
watch around midnight...

450
00:32:16,001 --> 00:32:18,027
The northern flank of
the herd, just like always...

451
00:32:18,170 --> 00:32:19,433
When the rain started.

452
00:32:19,571 --> 00:32:24,703
Let me tell you, it poured so hard, I
couldn't see 2 feet in front of my face.

453
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:31,072
Come morning, when the rain let
up, there was 20 head of them missing.

454
00:32:31,216 --> 00:32:33,981
I looked and I looked, but I'll
be damned if I could find them.

455
00:32:36,054 --> 00:32:40,219
A couple of days later, when I
was riding by Ned Salem's herd,

456
00:32:40,358 --> 00:32:42,038
I could have sworn I
saw a bunch of steers

457
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,061
with the Broken Rock
brand mixed in with his.

458
00:32:44,196 --> 00:32:45,789
So I told the sheriff.

459
00:32:46,898 --> 00:32:48,594
He rode out there
and took a look.

460
00:32:48,733 --> 00:32:50,702
He didn't see no
Broken Rock steers.

461
00:32:50,836 --> 00:32:52,304
That was the end of it.

462
00:32:52,437 --> 00:32:55,236
Any idea what happened to them?

463
00:32:55,373 --> 00:32:57,501
I guess maybe I just
plum made a mistake.

464
00:32:59,778 --> 00:33:01,679
Yeah, I guess you did.

465
00:33:03,381 --> 00:33:04,849
Um...

466
00:33:08,019 --> 00:33:11,915
Oh, could I...
Yeah. There you go.

467
00:33:15,527 --> 00:33:18,520
Now stand real
still. Stand real still.

468
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:19,995
Okay?

469
00:33:20,131 --> 00:33:22,532
Stand still now. Here I come.

470
00:33:24,069 --> 00:33:25,401
Bye.

471
00:33:26,805 --> 00:33:28,330
Come on, horse, come on.

472
00:33:28,473 --> 00:33:29,907
Come up here. Come up.

473
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:39,950
Hi.

474
00:33:40,952 --> 00:33:42,921
May I come in?

475
00:33:43,054 --> 00:33:45,614
Not if all you
want to do is talk.

476
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:48,989
This time I'm buying.

477
00:33:49,127 --> 00:33:52,586
Well, what are you standing
out there for? Come right in.

478
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:57,093
Well, that was
some fight, wasn't it?

479
00:34:02,173 --> 00:34:05,143
It was disgraceful.

480
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:08,839
I swear, I just don't know what
gets into you boys sometimes.

481
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:12,610
What did Rudy want?

482
00:34:12,751 --> 00:34:14,310
Rudy?

483
00:34:14,452 --> 00:34:18,321
The cowboy that started it.

484
00:34:18,456 --> 00:34:20,550
The same thing you want.

485
00:34:21,927 --> 00:34:24,624
He seemed determined to get it.

486
00:34:24,763 --> 00:34:30,760
Well, some men have
needs that just can't be denied.

487
00:34:33,672 --> 00:34:36,005
So he was just a customer?

488
00:34:38,009 --> 00:34:40,069
Just like you.

489
00:34:43,582 --> 00:34:46,074
Well, not exactly.

490
00:34:46,217 --> 00:34:47,913
You're leaving?

491
00:34:48,053 --> 00:34:53,788
Well, I said I was buying,
but I didn't say what.

492
00:35:13,945 --> 00:35:15,379
What will it be?

493
00:35:15,513 --> 00:35:17,914
Club soda with a lime.

494
00:35:27,225 --> 00:35:28,284
Whiskey.

495
00:35:34,599 --> 00:35:37,296
Something wrong with your drink?

496
00:35:37,435 --> 00:35:40,337
Smells like stain remover.

497
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:43,507
Want me to taste it for you?

498
00:35:55,086 --> 00:35:58,989
Tastes a little like stain
remover, but it's smooth.

499
00:36:02,594 --> 00:36:05,029
I don't get it. I
just don't get it.

500
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:09,624
Why would Michelle pay off Rudy?

501
00:36:09,768 --> 00:36:12,328
Rudy?

502
00:36:12,470 --> 00:36:17,841
Now, there's a walking testimony to
the goodness of man if I ever seen one.

503
00:36:17,976 --> 00:36:24,610
Just last week, he come walking down
the back stairs from Miss Michelle's room,

504
00:36:24,749 --> 00:36:29,881
sees me lying in the alley
trying to sleep in the pouring rain,

505
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:34,721
gives me a dollar so's I can spend the
rest of the night in the boarding house.

506
00:36:37,328 --> 00:36:44,326
The man's truly a monument
to charity and mercy.

507
00:36:44,469 --> 00:36:47,871
Here. Have another.

508
00:36:48,006 --> 00:36:49,599
Have it all.

509
00:36:49,741 --> 00:36:51,539
You're a genius.

510
00:36:51,676 --> 00:36:54,202
Thanks. I always thought so.

511
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:10,662
Would you like a ride?

512
00:37:10,795 --> 00:37:15,756
Oh, no, that's all right. I'm just
on my way to the boarding house.

513
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:18,927
- But on second thought...
- Whoa.

514
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:22,370
On second thought,
what the hell.

515
00:37:28,313 --> 00:37:33,445
I've been riding so much lately, I've
got bruises in places I've never seen.

516
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:36,384
This is a much more
civilized way to travel.

517
00:37:36,521 --> 00:37:38,717
- Your rig?
- Uh-huh.

518
00:37:38,857 --> 00:37:41,383
When I go somewhere,
I like to go in style.

519
00:37:41,526 --> 00:37:42,653
Do you like it?

520
00:37:42,794 --> 00:37:44,820
Yeah, it's nice.

521
00:37:44,963 --> 00:37:47,432
These cushions are real nice.

522
00:37:47,565 --> 00:37:48,999
Hello, Miss Michelle.

523
00:37:51,636 --> 00:37:53,366
Well, here we are.

524
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:57,572
Well, thanks for the lift.

525
00:37:57,709 --> 00:38:00,110
Should have known you
two would get together.

526
00:38:00,245 --> 00:38:02,612
Why, Miss Julie, I do
believe you're jealous.

527
00:38:11,456 --> 00:38:15,393
Well, the first thing I seen was Conrad
standing there with his gun in his hand.

528
00:38:15,527 --> 00:38:19,988
And the next thing I seen was the sheriff,
shot through the chest and dead as Moses.

529
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,895
Wasn't wearing
his gun or nothing.

530
00:38:22,033 --> 00:38:23,433
Where was his gun?

531
00:38:23,568 --> 00:38:25,400
Bottom desk drawer.

532
00:38:25,537 --> 00:38:28,234
Yeah, Conrad come in and shot
him before he could even get it open.

533
00:38:28,373 --> 00:38:30,501
Objection. Witness
is speculating.

534
00:38:30,642 --> 00:38:33,134
I know that. Sit down.

535
00:38:33,278 --> 00:38:35,804
Well, what about them?

536
00:38:35,947 --> 00:38:37,882
Well, they ain't standing up.

537
00:38:38,016 --> 00:38:41,885
I mean, aren't you going to tell
them to disregard what he just said?

538
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:44,319
Hell, look at them.
Half of them's asleep,

539
00:38:44,455 --> 00:38:47,175
the other half wouldn't know what
I was talking about if I told them.

540
00:38:47,292 --> 00:38:48,292
Now sit down.

541
00:38:48,359 --> 00:38:49,884
But, Your Honor...

542
00:38:50,028 --> 00:38:52,930
I've had about enough
of you, Mr. Matlock.

543
00:38:53,064 --> 00:38:55,795
I've got to be in Carson
City come sundown

544
00:38:55,934 --> 00:38:59,462
because at sunup I've got to
preside over Buck Macy's trial,

545
00:38:59,604 --> 00:39:01,266
because if he ain't
hung pretty quick,

546
00:39:01,406 --> 00:39:04,342
them outlaws he's running around
with is going to bust him out of jail,

547
00:39:04,475 --> 00:39:06,987
and a whole lot of people are
going to get killed in the process.

548
00:39:07,011 --> 00:39:08,741
Now, I can't get down there

549
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:13,147
if you keep jumping out of your chair
every 10 seconds like some jackrabbit.

550
00:39:13,284 --> 00:39:16,015
Now, I've had
enough. You sit down!

551
00:39:21,125 --> 00:39:23,253
How many times
was the sheriff shot?

552
00:39:23,394 --> 00:39:24,919
Once.

553
00:39:25,063 --> 00:39:27,760
And there was only one bullet
missing from Conrad's gun.

554
00:39:27,899 --> 00:39:29,697
Thank you. You can go sit.

555
00:39:29,834 --> 00:39:32,030
What about my cross-examination?

556
00:39:36,808 --> 00:39:38,743
I don't want a
cross-examination.

557
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:43,173
Anybody else got
anything to say?

558
00:39:43,314 --> 00:39:44,314
Yes, sir.

559
00:39:45,483 --> 00:39:48,419
May I call somebody
else to the stand?

560
00:39:48,553 --> 00:39:49,885
Who?

561
00:39:50,922 --> 00:39:52,356
Michelle Thomas.

562
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:10,407
Miss Michelle.

563
00:40:24,355 --> 00:40:29,123
I suppose a woman
in your profession

564
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:32,822
gets to know the cowboys
around here pretty well.

565
00:40:34,032 --> 00:40:35,933
That's one way of putting it.

566
00:40:36,067 --> 00:40:40,437
What they do, where they
work, when they ride watch.

567
00:40:40,571 --> 00:40:42,811
Most of them got better things
to do when they're with me

568
00:40:42,874 --> 00:40:45,105
than talk about their
jobs, Mr. Matlock.

569
00:40:45,243 --> 00:40:47,644
Yeah, but they tell
you, though, don't they?

570
00:40:47,779 --> 00:40:50,044
Sometimes, when they're
down here having a drink,

571
00:40:50,181 --> 00:40:52,946
especially when they ride watch?

572
00:40:53,084 --> 00:40:56,316
And then you pass that
information along to Ned Salem,

573
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:57,922
and then, between
the two of you,

574
00:40:58,056 --> 00:41:01,220
you decide which cowboy
you'll lure up to your room.

575
00:41:01,359 --> 00:41:04,022
And while he's busy
with you up there,

576
00:41:04,162 --> 00:41:08,065
Ned Salem and his boys are busy
helping themselves to the cattle

577
00:41:08,199 --> 00:41:11,294
that cowboy is supposed
to be watching, aren't they?

578
00:41:11,436 --> 00:41:13,735
That's the craziest
notion I've ever heard.

579
00:41:13,871 --> 00:41:17,000
It's so crazy, it worked
every time, didn't it?

580
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:20,600
Ned would sell the cattle right
away and give you your cut,

581
00:41:20,745 --> 00:41:24,546
and nobody ever knew because
the cowboys you got up to your room

582
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:28,915
were too embarrassed or afraid
of being fired to say anything.

583
00:41:30,588 --> 00:41:34,889
Until... Rudy came along.

584
00:41:35,026 --> 00:41:37,757
Now, as it happened,
Rudy was with you

585
00:41:37,895 --> 00:41:41,332
instead of watching a
Broken Rock herd that night.

586
00:41:41,466 --> 00:41:46,131
It rained last week, but
a couple of days later,

587
00:41:46,270 --> 00:41:48,671
he came across some
of those stolen cattle,

588
00:41:48,806 --> 00:41:51,970
only by now they were
part of Ned Salem's herd,

589
00:41:52,110 --> 00:41:56,741
so Rudy told the sheriff that he
thought you and Ned were in cahoots.

590
00:41:56,881 --> 00:42:02,149
Then the sheriff confronted you,
and soon thereafter, you shot him.

591
00:42:02,286 --> 00:42:05,347
Me? Shoot somebody?

592
00:42:05,490 --> 00:42:08,654
Why, I wouldn't even know
which end of a gun to point.

593
00:42:09,861 --> 00:42:13,161
And then Rudy confronted you,

594
00:42:13,297 --> 00:42:15,493
but you couldn't shoot him
right there in your room...

595
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:17,111
You wouldn't have
anybody to frame...

596
00:42:17,135 --> 00:42:20,936
So you paid him off with
a solid gold candlestick

597
00:42:21,072 --> 00:42:24,565
and made him promise to keep
his mouth shut about the cowboys,

598
00:42:24,709 --> 00:42:27,008
your relationship with Ned
Salem, and everything else.

599
00:42:27,145 --> 00:42:31,810
And he was all prepared
to do that until last night,

600
00:42:31,949 --> 00:42:36,649
when I explained to
him what perjury means.

601
00:42:36,788 --> 00:42:43,922
Now, if I put him where you're sitting,
Miss Thomas, he's not going to lie.

602
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:48,500
Mr. Matlock, I don't reckon
that half the people in this room

603
00:42:48,633 --> 00:42:54,834
know what the word conjecture
means, but I do, and I've had enough.

604
00:42:54,972 --> 00:42:58,909
Now, either you prove what you're
saying, or stop saying it and sit down!

605
00:42:59,043 --> 00:43:00,909
Proof, right. Proof.

606
00:43:01,045 --> 00:43:05,813
Believe it or not, that's
just what I was coming to.

607
00:43:07,018 --> 00:43:08,762
Gunshots! Sounds like
it's coming from the jail.

608
00:43:08,786 --> 00:43:10,880
Hold it, hold it, hold
it, hold it, hold it.

609
00:43:11,022 --> 00:43:13,457
Everything is all
right. Everything's fine.

610
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:17,028
See, that's just Bob shooting
Conrad's gun off over at the jail.

611
00:43:17,161 --> 00:43:19,096
- See?
- Order.

612
00:43:19,230 --> 00:43:21,961
Order in the court!
Everybody back here!

613
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:24,001
Everybody back
here and sit down!

614
00:43:24,135 --> 00:43:27,731
I've always wondered why
nobody heard the fatal shot.

615
00:43:27,872 --> 00:43:30,000
Yet you all heard
that shot just now.

616
00:43:30,141 --> 00:43:33,236
You even had a pretty good
idea where it came from.

617
00:43:33,377 --> 00:43:36,279
So why didn't
anybody hear it then?

618
00:43:36,414 --> 00:43:38,007
I'll tell you.

619
00:43:40,785 --> 00:43:42,083
Here's why.

620
00:43:43,521 --> 00:43:46,047
Would you tell the
judge what this is, Tom?

621
00:43:46,190 --> 00:43:49,024
Well, it looks like one of those
cushions off Miss Michelle's buggy.

622
00:43:49,160 --> 00:43:50,160
That's right.

623
00:43:50,294 --> 00:43:53,162
Jake King watched
me take it off her buggy

624
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:55,476
over at the livery stable this
morning, didn't you, Jake?

625
00:43:55,500 --> 00:44:00,097
This is why you
didn't hear the shot.

626
00:44:00,238 --> 00:44:01,729
The other afternoon,

627
00:44:01,873 --> 00:44:06,243
when Conrad came in here
wearing his gun, looking for the sheriff,

628
00:44:06,377 --> 00:44:08,778
you went and got this
cushion, didn't you?

629
00:44:08,913 --> 00:44:12,748
And you also got a gun, and
you went over to the sheriff's office,

630
00:44:12,884 --> 00:44:16,685
and not only was the sheriff still
alive, but Conrad was unconscious,

631
00:44:16,821 --> 00:44:22,351
and you saw your opportunity,
and you put your gun into this pillow

632
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:26,123
and fired through it so no one
could hear the shot and come running.

633
00:44:26,264 --> 00:44:30,599
And then, with the sheriff
dead, you walked over to Conrad,

634
00:44:30,735 --> 00:44:34,968
took one bullet out of his pistol,
and put the gun in his hand.

635
00:44:35,106 --> 00:44:37,439
Then you slipped out
without anybody seeing you.

636
00:44:37,575 --> 00:44:40,443
And finally, you put this
cushion back in your buggy,

637
00:44:40,578 --> 00:44:41,841
thinking no one would notice.

638
00:44:41,979 --> 00:44:49,751
But I noticed yesterday, when you
were so kind to give me that ride.

639
00:44:49,887 --> 00:44:50,887
There.

640
00:44:50,922 --> 00:44:52,117
Here, here, here.

641
00:44:52,256 --> 00:44:54,657
Order, order!

642
00:44:56,327 --> 00:44:57,886
All right, don't nobody move.

643
00:44:58,896 --> 00:45:00,990
- Now, see here, young lady.
- Sit down!

644
00:45:03,134 --> 00:45:04,796
Now, I'm leaving here,

645
00:45:04,936 --> 00:45:08,373
and if anybody tries to stop
me, the lawyer here gets a bullet.

646
00:45:08,506 --> 00:45:10,668
- Get out of my way.
- Nope.

647
00:45:10,808 --> 00:45:13,300
I'll kill him, I swear I will.
I've got nothing to lose.

648
00:45:13,444 --> 00:45:16,312
- Let her go!
- She makes a good point, Tom.

649
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:18,848
- Move.
- Nope.

650
00:45:23,554 --> 00:45:26,217
Ohh! No. Oh.

651
00:45:26,357 --> 00:45:27,985
Ben, are you all right?

652
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:30,823
What happened?

653
00:45:30,962 --> 00:45:33,625
That sign came loose and
whacked you on the head.

654
00:45:36,267 --> 00:45:37,530
You're alive.

655
00:45:38,636 --> 00:45:40,002
Of course I'm alive.

656
00:45:40,137 --> 00:45:42,299
You've been out cold, Ben.

657
00:45:43,774 --> 00:45:45,072
The mechanic's here.

658
00:45:45,209 --> 00:45:48,611
Wait, wait. Don't get
up. You should rest.

659
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:49,746
- That's all right.
- Ben?

660
00:45:49,814 --> 00:45:55,754
That's okay. I can get... I can get
plenty of rest on the stagecoach.

661
00:45:57,755 --> 00:45:59,656
I mean... I mean the bus.

662
00:46:10,334 --> 00:46:12,496
Excuse me, sir.

663
00:46:12,637 --> 00:46:15,334
How long do you think it will
take for you to get us rolling again?

664
00:46:15,473 --> 00:46:17,635
I don't know. Now get
on the bus and sit down.

665
00:46:17,775 --> 00:46:21,542
- She just asked you a simple question.
- Ohh!

666
00:46:21,679 --> 00:46:25,309
Look, I've got to be in
Carson City come sunup

667
00:46:25,449 --> 00:46:27,249
because another one of
these buses broke down,

668
00:46:27,351 --> 00:46:31,288
and if I don't fix it, there's going
to be one mad busload of tourists.

669
00:46:31,422 --> 00:46:33,516
Now, a man's got to do
what a man's got to do,

670
00:46:33,658 --> 00:46:35,923
so get on the bus and sit down!

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
